  "description": "Find the length of the longest subarray such that the absolute difference between any two elements is less than or equal to limit.",
  "target": 2,
  "pseudocode": "1. left = 0, maxLen = 0\n2. minQ = [], maxQ = []\n3. for right = 0 to nums.length - 1:\n4.   while minQ and nums[minQ.back] >= nums[right]: minQ.pop()\n5.   while maxQ and nums[maxQ.back] <= nums[right]: maxQ.pop()\n6.   minQ.push(right), maxQ.push(right)\n7.   while nums[maxQ[0]] - nums[minQ[0]] > limit:\n8.     left++\n9.     if minQ[0] < left: minQ.shift()\n10.    if maxQ[0] < left: maxQ.shift()\n11.  maxLen = max(maxLen, right - left + 1)",
